    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ENUM-STYLE STATES\n\nBlueprints have no dedicated enum type: the usual pattern is an integer where each number stands\nfor a named state, plus a Switch On Int to act on it. Agree on the numbers in one place (this box):\n    0 = Idle     1 = Walking     2 = Jumping     3 = Falling\nA For Loop advances the state three times with (state + 1) mod 4, and a custom event 'Describe'\nturns the number into a name every time.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          230.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "ADVANCE THE STATE\nstate = (state + 1) mod 4, three times: 1, 2, 3. After each step the Describe event is dispatched with the new state.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "NAME THE STATE\nSwitch On Int sends 0..3 to Case0..Case3 (anything else to Default). Each case stores and prints the name. The last pass leaves label = \"Falling\".",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          1030.0
        ],
        "size": [
          960.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
